# Copy to .env.local (never commit .env.local).
# With this key set, /plan uses real Google Places + Routes data.
# Without it, the app runs entirely on the mock catalog in fixtures/.
#
# Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services:
#   1. Enable "Places API (New)" and "Routes API"
#   2. Create an API key (restrict it to those two APIs)
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# SEPARATE key for the browser map. It is public by nature — never reuse the
# server key above, which carries Places and Routes quota.
#   Enable ONLY: Maps JavaScript API
#   Restrict by HTTP referrer to your domain + http://localhost:3000/*
# Leave blank: the place picker falls back to a list and nothing breaks.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_BROWSER_KEY=

# Where saved plans live, so a share link survives a restart. Vercel's Postgres
# integrations set POSTGRES_URL for you; DATABASE_URL is accepted too.
#   Vercel → Storage → Neon (free tier is enough), then pull it locally with
#   `vercel env pull .env.local`.
# Leave blank: plans fall back to memory and die with the server process, which
# on serverless means a share link 404s almost immediately.
POSTGRES_URL=
